# Cab Lab usage log (read before guessing)

When the user reports something that went wrong in The Cab Lab (box placed at the wrong place, wrong size, inference not engaging, handle drag misbehaving, crash, file not opening…), **read the log first**; do not ask them to re-describe coordinates or steps.

## Files (all under `the-cab-lab/logs/`, git-ignored)

1. `latest.json` — last action and last error of the current session. Start here.
2. `usage.jsonl` — append-only event stream, one JSON object per line (`seq`, `t`, `kind`, …). Read the last ~50 lines; the event the user is talking about is normally the last `place.finish` / `handle.end` / `error`.
3. `crash-<time>.json` — full `job.json` + cursor trace written on `window.error` / unhandled rejection.

`Ctrl+Shift+L` in the app opens this folder.

## Event kinds

- `session.start` — version, viewport.
- `place.arm` / `place.anchor` / `place.face` / `place.corner` / `place.typein` / `place.trace` / `place.finish` / `place.repeat` / `place.cancel` / `place.blocked` / `place.unfit` — one box placement in three steps (anchor on a face → opposite corner of a flat rectangle on that face → extrude along the face normal, away from the solid only). Side walls are only pickable from the room inside. `place.anchor` / `place.face` carry `plane` `{axis, value, dir, label}` (`place.face` = a corner anchor switched to the face being drawn over). `place.finish` carries `how` (click / enter / `*.preset` / click.locked / repeat), `anchor`, `corner`, `locked` (typed dims), `plane`, `extrude` (`len`, snap `label`), `clamped` (dims stopped by the space, with the wall name) and the final `box` (x0/y0/z0/W/D/H). `place.trace` is the last 60 cursor samples: `cx/cy` client px, `x/y/z` resolved world mm, `kind` = `feature` | `inference` | `align` | `plane` | `extrude` | `extrude.snap` (with `len`, `label`), `dir`, `shift`.
- `move.start` / `move.grab` / `move.typein` / `move.trace` / `move.finish` / `move.copy` / `move.cancel` — the Move command (grab point → target point, ΔX/ΔY/ΔZ, clamped list).
- `orient.start` / `orient.pending` / `orient.blocked` / `orient.end` / `orient.cancel` — the Face command (`face` `{axis, dir, label}` clicked, `from` / `to` `{pose, envelope}` — the box never moves, W/D swap; `blocked` = side against a wall / neighbour, `small` = W/D under the module minimum; `how` = click / enter, `changed`).
- `place.finish` also carries `side` `{axis, dir}` (door side chosen: never against a wall / neighbour, else long edge toward the room), `size` `{W, D, H}` in module terms and the resulting `pose`.
- Overhead (`moduleId: overheadCabinet`, ceiling-hung): `place.anchor` carries `walls` (the ceiling ∩ wall lines the anchor sits on) and `term` (`{x, y, z}` → which module dimension W/D/H runs along each world axis once the back wall is known); `place.face` carries `term` too; `place.finish` carries `wall` (the back wall's label; W runs along it, doors face away from it). `place.blocked` with `reason: "not on a ceiling edge"` = the click was not on a feature point of a ceiling ∩ wall line (only those can start an overhead). At a corner the back wall is decided at the end: the wall the longer horizontal edge follows.
- `orient.blocked` with `reason: "module has a fixed door side"` / `key.rotate` with `blocked` — Face and `R` are refused on an overhead. Move on an overhead always logs `delta.z` 0.
- `ohc.zone.select` / `ohc.zone.drag` (`boundary`, `changed`, `widths` — one boundary drag on the strip, one undo step) / `ohc.zone.type` (`zone`, `type`) / `ohc.zone.width` / `ohc.zone.add` / `ohc.zone.remove` (`removed`) / `ohc.zone.average` (`zones`) / `ohc.zone.blocked` — the overhead editor page (right panel). `widths` always sum to `cabinetWidth`; none is under 150. A "wrong zone" report is normally the last of these plus the `handle.end` of a vertical divider bar (`zones` there lists widths for an overhead).
- `retype.start` / `retype.typein` / `retype.end` / `retype.cancel` — digits re-sizing the last created box while still armed.
- `nose.arm` / `nose.drag` / `nose.typein` / `nose.finish` / `nose.cancel` — Bedroom (nose slab) placement: `arm` carries `depth` (preset 700 or the existing slab's) and `editId` (non-null = the module was picked again and the existing slab is being re-sized, nothing is duplicated); `drag` = the click that started the room-side face following the cursor; `finish` carries `how` (click / enter), `depth`, `locked`, `snap` (label), `clamped` (`back wall` / `minimum N` / a cabinet id), `edited`, `changed`, `pose` (always `rotZ 180`, `y = depth`), `envelope` and the bound `roofProfile` (local Y from the room face). Width / height of the slab are never typed: they come from the space, so a "wrong height" is a space (roof profile) question, not a placement one.
- `bedbox.arm` / `bedbox.blocked` / `bedbox.width` / `bedbox.typein` / `bedbox.finish` / `bedbox.cancel` — Bed Box placement (needs the Bedroom body: `blocked` = no body). `arm` carries `editId` (non-null = re-sizing the existing one), `bodyId`, `bodyDepth` and the starting `W/D/H`; `width` = the click / Enter that locked the width (`W`, `locked`, `clamped` `side walls` / `minimum N`); `finish` carries `how`, `W`, `D`, `H` (420 = tunnel boot), `locked`, `snap`, `clamped` (`back wall` / `minimum N` / a cabinet id in the bed's lane), `edited`, `changed`, `pose` (`rotZ 180`, `x = centre + W/2`, `y = bodyDepth + D`). X is never typed or dragged: the box is always centred on the van, so an "off-centre bed" is a space-width or body question.
- `plane.arm` / `plane.blocked` / `plane.face` / `plane.typein` / `plane.finish` / `plane.cancel` / `plane.add` / `plane.remove` — construction plane: click a wall or cabinet face, offset a parallel copy into the room (`dir` of the source face). `face` carries `axis/value/dir/label/source/room`; `finish` / `add` carry `id`, `axis`, `value` (world), `offset`, `from` `{source, label}`. The plane is world-fixed (does not follow the source). Its outline vertices (plane ∩ space) are snap points. `blocked` = no space, or the face has no room outward.
- `rail.group.open` — a rail group's flyout (Bedroom → Body / Bed Box / Bed Side Table) opened on hover or click.
- `cabinet.add` / `cabinet.remove` / `cabinet.params` / `cabinet.pose` / `select` / `key.delete` / `key.rotate`.
- `handle.start` / `handle.end` — W/D/H face or `divider` drags with envelope before/after, zones and pose.
- `space.dialog.open` / `space.dialog.close` / `space.dialog.kind` / `space.dialog.choice` / `space.define` — `values` carries the whole form (vehicle: `width`, `rearDepth`, `height`, `frontMode`, `front.points` / `front.dxf.points` as `[y, z]` mm). `space.define` / dialog open+close also carry job-level `finish` (`carcass` White Stipple; `door.series` acrylic|hpl; `door.mode` one|two; `door.colors` `[{id, series, name}]`) and `stock` (`carcass` / `partition` / `door` thicknesses). `space.dialog.choice` on the catalogue uses `key` `finish.door.series` or `finish.door.mode`.
- `materials.set` — the job catalogue was written (`finish`, `stock`). Existing cabinets keep the thicknesses they already copied; new ones inherit.
- `materials.default.set` / `materials.default.reset` — "Set current as default" for colours + board stocks: `ok`, `path` (settings.json), `error`, `finish`, `stock`.
- `space.dxf.import` — `ok`, `path`, `points`, `chains`, `units`, `scale`, `counts` per entity type, `warnings`, `range` `{y, z}`; or `error`.
- `space.default.set` / `space.default.reset` — "Set current as default" for a space kind: `ok`, `path` (settings.json), `error`, `values`.
- `settings.loaded` / `settings.corrupt` / `settings.read.failed` / `settings.write.failed` — user settings file (`<userData>/settings.json`); a corrupt file falls back to built-in defaults and is left in place.
- Placement / move `clamped` may name `roof` (the sloped nose of a vehicle) instead of `ceiling`.
- `file.new` / `file.open` / `file.open.failed` / `file.save`, `undo` / `redo`, `view`.
- **Generator bench** (`docs/bench-spec.md`; separate window, developer tool): `bench.open` (`module`, `preset`, `from` rail|cabinet|env|tab, `custom`), `bench.tab`, `bench.preset`, `bench.preset.save`, `bench.param` (`key`, `from`, `to`), `bench.select` (`what` board|face|point|joint|key, `id`, `key` / `keys`, `value`, `formula`), `bench.tryout` (`key`, `formula`, `expr`, `from`, `to` — a what-if on one value; nothing was changed), `bench.rule.set` (`name`, `from`, `to`, **`reason`**, `affected` keys, `boards`, `path` — rules.json **was** rewritten), `bench.rebuild` (`ok`, `ms`), `bench.pin` (`preset`, `what` board|all, `id`, `count`, `faces`), `bench.report` (`path` of `logs/bench/<time>-<module>.md`, `selection`, `note`), `bench.board.open` / `bench.board.frame`, `bench.view`.
  - When asked to fix a generator dimension: read the newest `logs/bench/*.md` first — it names the board / point, its provenance chain (`value = formula (terms)`), what was tried and what the user expects. Then `bench.rule.set` entries: the `reason` is the user's design intent; keep it. Pinned values (`generators/<module>/presets.json`) are the protected numbers; run the generator test after any change.
- `generator.errors` — generator `validation.errors` for a cabinet.
- `error` / `console.error` — with stack.

## Rules

- Quote the relevant entries (seq + kind + the numbers) when explaining a cause.
- If the files are missing or the last entry is older than the user's report, say so; do not invent events.
- Log payloads are plain JSON; never contain Three.js objects.
